  "faqAlarmsQIos": "How do I set up alarms, and what’s the notification permission?",
  "faqAlarmsAIos": "In Settings › Alarms, turn on “Alert before each shift”, choose how long before and, if you like, an alert the day before at a set time. In a day’s details you can remove its alarm with “No alarm this day”.\n\nWithout notification permission, Cuadrante can’t alert you. If the window to allow them doesn’t appear, turn them on in the system settings.",
  "faqWidgetAIos": "In Settings › Add widget you’ll see the sizes (small: today and tomorrow; medium: the next 7 days; large: the whole month) and how to place it. Touch and hold the home screen, tap the + at the top and look for Cuadrante.\n\nThe widget stores your upcoming days. The system decides when to update it and may delay the change of day. If it runs out of data, open Cuadrante to bring it up to date.",
  "faqBackupAIos": "Settings › Backup saves automatic backups on this device after each change, but they are lost if you lose it or uninstall the app. Export a file with “Export file” and save it to iCloud Drive or send it to yourself by WhatsApp or email.\n\nTo change devices: export the file, install Cuadrante on the new device, open the file with the app (or use “Import file” in Backup), and review the preview before restoring. “Test restore” checks that your latest backup can be fully recovered.",
  "calExportPermissionDeniedBodyIos": "Turn it on in the system settings (Cuadrante › Calendars) and come back here.",
  "backupUiWarningIos": "These backups are kept on this device. If you uninstall the app without another copy, it’s lost. Export a file and save it to iCloud Drive or send it by WhatsApp or email.",
